&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Strategic Finance- Go-to-Market&lt;/strong&gt; to be the lead finance partner for our Enterprise and Mid-Market businesses across Sales, Account Mgmt, Customer Success, and Marketing. You&#39;ll sit at the center of how we scale two distinct, high-performing sales motions,&amp;nbsp; translating business performance into clear financial insights and driving the decisions that drive top-line growth. This role is highly visible, with regular collaboration with our executive team and the opportunity to shape strategy to increase market share.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership &amp;amp; Business Partnership: &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as the lead strategic finance partner to executives across our GTM teams. Build trusted relationships that make you a go-to thought partner on the decisions that matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the next-generation StratFin team:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop AI-powered workflows, automated analyses, and intelligence systems that redefine what a strategic finance team can do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy: &lt;/strong&gt;Assess current and future strategic priorities. Quantitatively validate and advocate for the highest-ROI initiatives across the GTM organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insights: &lt;/strong&gt;Proactively deliver data-driven recommendations that inform go-to-market tactics, product experiments, and cross-functional roadmaps. Build frameworks for evaluating sales efficiency and productivity. Partner with Data Analytics to develop predictive and automated reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Planning: &lt;/strong&gt;Own a significant portion of our long-range and annual planning processes, including the strategic plan that positions GTM to hit our growth goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team: &lt;/strong&gt;Develop and grow a high-performing analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of progressive experience, including 4+ years covering sales. Foundational experience in investment banking, private equity, or management consulting preferred. Experience with consumption-based business models is a meaningful plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving measurable business outcomes through financial analysis and strategic insight, not just reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success driving sales strategy, planning, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built something with AI- a model, a workflow, an automated analysis. You&#39;re eager to do more of it. You see AI as a core part of how great finance teams will operate, not a novelty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level modeling ability, translating complex business drivers into clear frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence. You communicate with clarity and conviction at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce, BI tools (ie. Omni), SQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You identify problems before they&#39;re handed to you, and you thrive when the answer isn&#39;t obvious.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An A-player mindset with a strong bias for action: you raise the bar, move with urgency, stay resilient through ambiguity, and take ownership to deliver meaningful outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
